<Base title="MuTechLab | Music Technology in Music Education, University of Luxembourg" description="MuTechLab, an initiative of the University of Luxembourg, promotes technology in music performance and education, training music teachers in dialogue with music students." path="/">
  <div class="page">
<p>Dear Music teachers and students</p><p class=gap>Welcome to the <strong><span class="blue">MuTechLab</span></strong> website.</p><p class=gap><strong><span class="blue">MuTechLab</span> </strong>is an initiative taken by the Institute of Musicology and the Arts at the <strong><span class="orange"><a href="http://www.uni.lu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Luxembourg</a></span></strong>.</p><p>The objective of MuTechLab is to promote the use of technology in music performance and education, with a focus on training pre- and in-service music teachers in dialogue with music students.</p><p class=gap>A key rationale for the project is to integrate a range of technologies into musicians’ identities as performers, thereby fostering the broader incorporation of educational technology.</p><p class=gap>A first initiative was the<span class="blue"> <strong><a href="/fnr">FNR-funded PSP-Classic project</a></strong></span>.</p><p>MuTechLab has now become a course in the Bachelor in Music Education.</p><p>We are currently working on a certificate program for BEM graduates and in-service teachers.</p><p class=gap>More projects will follow in the near future!</p>
  </div>
</Base>
